         ],
         [
-          "La diplomática se puso nerviosa durante el debate televisivo.",
-          "The diplomat became nervous during the televised debate."
+          "Se quedó callada durante toda la cena.",
+          "She stayed quiet for the whole dinner. (the state)"
         ],
         [
-          "Tras el terremoto, miles de familias se quedaron sin hogar.",
-          "After the earthquake, thousands of families were left homeless."
+          "La noticia nos puso muy tristes.",
+          "The news made us very sad. (the cause is the subject)"
         ],
         [
-          "El público se quedó boquiabierto ante la elocuencia de la oradora.",
-          "The audience was left agape at the speaker's eloquence."
+          "Los trabajadores se quedaron sin empleo.",
+          "The workers were left without jobs. (the result)"
+        ],
+        [
+          "Al ver el precio, se puso pálido y se quedó sin palabras.",
+          "On seeing the price, he turned pale and was left speechless. (both)"
         ]
       ]
     },
+    {
+      "type": "examples",
+      "title": "In context",
+      "items": [
+        {
+          "spanish": "Mi hermano se puso rojo de vergüenza.",
+          "english": "My brother went red with embarrassment."
+        },
+        {
+          "spanish": "Cuando entró el jefe, todos nos quedamos callados.",
+          "english": "When the boss came in, we all fell silent."
+        },
+        {
+          "spanish": "Se puso a llorar.",
