+      "content": "You know *llegar a ser* from B1 Unit 39: the high point of a long effort (*llegó a ser presidente de la compañía*). At B2 you use it in more places. Like any verb, it can follow *querer* or *poder* (*quiero llegar a ser*, *puede llegar a ser*), and it can also describe a thing that grows into something important: *La tienda llegó a ser una gran empresa*. It always carries the idea of a path: time, effort and steps. That is the difference from *convertirse en* (the thing becomes completely new) and from *hacerse* (you simply become, with no sense of a high point). In this lesson *llegar a* always comes with *ser*."
     },
